{"name": "Flashcard Forge", "html": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Flashcard Forge — MyLLMos™ App Gallery · © 2026 Opticell Ltd\n  Source-available: read it, remix it, run your version inside MyLLM™.\n  Not for redistribution or republication. Terms: https://github.com/TeamDzX/myllm-assets/blob/main/LICENSE\n--><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Flashcard Forge</title>\n<style>\n:root{--build-id:\"a1c4935400\";\n  color-scheme:light dark;\n  --font:var(--myllm-font,-apple-system,system-ui,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif);\n  --page1:#eef1f8; --page2:#eef6ff;\n  --surface:#ffffff; --surface2:#f3f4fa;\n  --ink:#191c28; --muted:#697083; --faint:#a2a8b8;\n  --border:#e7e9f1;\n  --acc:#635bff; --acc2:#22a7f0; --accSoft:rgba(99,91,255,.12);\n  --radius:16px; --radiusLg:22px;\n  --shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(20,20,50,.05),0 8px 22px -14px rgba(30,40,110,.28);\n  --shadowLg:0 16px 44px -16px rgba(40,50,150,.5);\n}\n@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){:root{\n  --page1:#0b0d13; --page2:#0d1220;\n  --surface:#181b24; --surface2:#20232f;\n  --ink:#f1f2f7; --muted:#9aa0af; --faint:#666d7d;\n  --border:#282c39; --accSoft:rgba(99,91,255,.22);\n  --shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.4),0 10px 28px -14px rgba(0,0,0,.7);\n  --shadowLg:0 18px 48px -16px rgba(0,0,0,.85);\n}}\n*{box-sizing:border-box;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent}\nbody{font-family:var(--font);margin:0;padding:18px 16px calc(34px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));\n  background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--page1),var(--page2));background-attachment:fixed;\n  min-height:100dvh;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.4}\n@media(min-width:768px){body{max-width:720px;margin:0 auto}}\n\n.hero{position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--radiusLg);padding:20px;margin-bottom:16px;\n  background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--acc),var(--acc2));color:#fff;box-shadow:var(--shadowLg);\n  display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px}\n.hero::after{content:\"\";position:absolute;right:-46px;top:-46px;width:170px;height:170px;border-radius:50%;\n  background:radial-gradient(circle,rgba(255,255,255,.28),transparent 70%);pointer-events:none}\n.hero-badge{width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:16px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.22);\n  display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:28px;flex:0 0 auto}\n.hero h1{font-size:22px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin:0}\n.hero p{margin:3px 0 0;font-size:13px;opacity:.92;font-weight:500}\n\n.surface{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radiusLg);\n  padding:16px;box-shadow:var(--shadow);margin-bottom:16px}\n.field{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;background:var(--surface2);border:1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius:13px;padding:0 13px;margin-bottom:10px}\n.field-ic{font-size:16px;opacity:.7;flex:0 0 auto}\n.field input{flex:1;border:0;background:none;padding:13px 0;font-size:16px;color:var(--ink);\n  outline:none;min-width:0;font-family:var(--font)}\n.field input::placeholder{color:var(--faint)}\n.btn-primary{width:100%;border:0;border-radius:14px;padding:14px;font-size:15px;font-weight:700;color:#fff;\n  font-family:var(--font);background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--acc),var(--acc2));\n  box-shadow:0 8px 20px -8px var(--acc);cursor:pointer;transition:transform .1s,opacity .2s}\n.btn-primary:active{transform:scale(.98)}\n.btn-primary:disabled{opacity:.5;box-shadow:none}\n.btn-ghost{width:100%;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:13px;padding:11px;font-size:13.5px;\n  font-weight:650;color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--font);background:var(--surface);cursor:pointer;\n  margin-bottom:12px;transition:transform .1s}\n.btn-ghost:active{transform:scale(.98)}\n.chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:7px;margin:2px 0 12px}\n.chip{border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface);color:var(--muted);border-radius:999px;\n  padding:7px 12px;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font);transition:.15s}\n.chip.on{color:var(--acc);border-color:var(--acc);background:var(--accSoft)}\n.status{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);min-height:18px;margin-top:9px;text-align:center}\n\n/* active-deck header — makes it obvious what you're studying */\n.deck-head{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin:2px 2px 14px}\n.deck-head .badge{width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:13px;flex:0 0 auto;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:22px;\n  color:#fff;background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--acc),var(--acc2));box-shadow:0 6px 16px -8px var(--acc)}\n.deck-head .dt{font-size:18px;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:-.01em;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}\n.deck-head .dm{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:1px}\n\n/* flip card */\n#study{display:none}\n.card{perspective:1400px;cursor:pointer;margin-bottom:13px}\n.card-inner{position:relative;height:216px;transition:transform .55s cubic-bezier(.2,.75,.2,1);transform-style:preserve-3d}\n.card-inner.flipped{transform:rotateY(180deg)}\n.face{position:absolute;inset:0;backface-visibility:hidden;-webkit-backface-visibility:hidden;\n  display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;\n  border-radius:var(--radiusLg);padding:26px 22px;overflow-y:auto}\n.face.front{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);box-shadow:var(--shadowLg)}\n.face.back{background:linear-gradient(150deg,var(--acc),var(--acc2));color:#fff;transform:rotateY(180deg);box-shadow:var(--shadowLg)}\n.face-label{font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;opacity:.5;margin-bottom:12px}\n.face.back .face-label{opacity:.85}\n.face-text{font-size:19px;line-height:1.45;font-weight:600}\n.face-tip{position:absolute;bottom:11px;left:0;right:0;font-size:11px;opacity:.4;font-weight:500}\n\n.sizerow{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:10px;margin:2px 0 12px}\n/* the chips wrap on narrow screens, so the label pins to the first row rather\n   than floating to the centre of a two-row group */\n.sizelbl{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--muted);letter-spacing:.02em;flex:0 0 auto;\n  min-width:42px;padding-top:9px}\n.chips.tight{margin:0;gap:6px}\n\n/* ---- fullscreen study ----\n   iOS WKWebView does not honour requestFullscreen for anything but video, so\n   immersion is an in-page layer that owns the viewport. requestFullscreen is\n   still attempted underneath, which buys real fullscreen in a desktop browser\n   and costs nothing where it is unsupported. */\n.fs{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:200;display:none;flex-direction:column;\n  background:linear-gradient(180deg,var(--page1),var(--page2));\n  padding:calc(10px + env(safe-area-inset-top)) 16px calc(14px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom))}\n.fs.on{display:flex}\nbody.fs-open{overflow:hidden}\n.fs-top{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex:0 0 auto;padding-bottom:10px}\n.fs-topic{font-size:14px;font-weight:750;letter-spacing:-.01em;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;\n  text-overflow:ellipsis;min-width:0;flex:1}\n.fs-count{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:650;color:var(--muted);flex:0 0 auto;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.fs-x{flex:0 0 auto;width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:11px;border:1px solid var(--border);\n  background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);font-size:15px;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font)}\n.fs-bar{height:4px;border-radius:3px;background:var(--border);overflow:hidden;flex:0 0 auto;margin-bottom:12px}\n.fs-bar i{display:block;height:100%;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--acc),var(--acc2));\n  border-radius:3px;transition:width .28s cubic-bezier(.2,.75,.2,1)}\n.fs-stage{flex:1;min-height:0;perspective:1600px;cursor:pointer;touch-action:pan-y;\n  display:flex;align-items:center}\n/* Filling every pixel of a tall phone leaves the words marooned in a wall of\n   colour, so the card keeps a comfortable reading proportion and centres. */\n.fs-stage .card-inner{height:min(100%,72vh);width:100%}\n.fs-stage .face-text{font-size:clamp(22px,5.4vw,34px);line-height:1.34}\n.fs-stage .face{padding:34px 26px}\n.fs-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-top:13px;flex:0 0 auto}\n.fs-nav button{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--ink);border-radius:13px;\n  padding:13px 22px;font-weight:700;font-size:15px;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font);transition:transform .1s}\n.fs-nav button:active{transform:scale(.96)}\n.fs-hint{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--faint);font-weight:600;text-align:center}\n\n/* grading row — only ever shown once the answer is face-up, because grading\n   a card you haven't seen the back of is meaningless */\n.grades{display:none;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:7px;margin:0 0 12px}\n.grades.on{display:grid}\n.grade{border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface);border-radius:12px;padding:9px 4px;\n  cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font);display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:2px;\n  transition:transform .1s}\n.grade:active{transform:scale(.95)}\n.grade b{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:750;color:var(--ink)}\n.grade span{font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--faint);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.grade.g0 b{color:#d2544e}.grade.g1 b{color:#d08a2e}\n.grade.g2 b{color:#2f9e5e}.grade.g3 b{color:var(--acc)}\n.fs .grades{margin-bottom:10px}\n\n.srcrow{display:flex;gap:7px;margin-bottom:12px}\n.src{flex:1;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface);color:var(--muted);border-radius:12px;\n  padding:9px;font-size:13px;font-weight:650;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font);transition:.15s}\n.src.on{color:var(--acc);border-color:var(--acc);background:var(--accSoft)}\n#srcNotes textarea{width:100%;background:var(--surface2);border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--ink);\n  border-radius:14px;padding:12px 13px;font-family:var(--font);font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;\n  resize:vertical;margin-bottom:6px}\n#srcNotes textarea:focus{outline:2px solid var(--acc);outline-offset:-1px}\n.notemeta{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--faint);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:10px;text-align:right}\n\n.headfs{margin-left:auto;flex:0 0 auto;width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:11px;\n  border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface);color:var(--muted);font-size:15px;\n  cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font)}\n.headfs:active{transform:scale(.95)}\n\n/* Deck tools collapse. Six buttons stacked between the card and Prev/Next\n   pushed navigation off the bottom of the screen — the thing you press on\n   every single card was the hardest thing to reach. Navigation now sits\n   directly under the card, and the occasional actions fold away. */\n.tools{margin:2px 0 14px}\n.toolsbtn{width:100%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:7px;\n  border:1px solid var(--border);background:transparent;color:var(--muted);border-radius:12px;\n  padding:9px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:650;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font)}\n.toolsbtn:active{transform:scale(.99)}\n.toolsbtn .caret{font-size:10px;transition:transform .2s}\n.toolsbtn.open{color:var(--acc);border-color:var(--acc)}\n.toolsbtn.open .caret{transform:rotate(180deg)}\n.toolsbody{padding-top:11px}\n\n.cardacts{display:flex;gap:8px;margin:0 0 12px}\n.cardacts button{flex:1;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface);color:var(--muted);\n  border-radius:12px;padding:9px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:650;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font);\n  transition:transform .1s}\n.cardacts button:active{transform:scale(.97)}\n.cardacts button.on{color:var(--acc);border-color:var(--acc);background:var(--accSoft)}\n\n.editor{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radiusLg);\n  padding:18px;margin-bottom:14px;box-shadow:var(--shadow)}\n.ed-t{font-size:15px;font-weight:750;margin-bottom:12px}\n.ed-l{display:block;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;\n  letter-spacing:.06em;margin:0 0 5px}\n.editor textarea{width:100%;background:var(--surface2);border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--ink);\n  border-radius:12px;padding:11px 12px;font-family:var(--font);font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.45;\n  resize:vertical;margin-bottom:12px}\n.editor textarea:focus{outline:2px solid var(--acc);outline-offset:-1px}\n.ed-row{display:flex;gap:9px}\n.ed-row .btn-primary{margin:0;flex:1}\n.ed-row .btn-ghost{flex:1}\n.ed-msg{font-size:12.5px;color:#d2544e;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px;min-height:0}\n.ed-del{width:100%;margin-top:10px;background:none;border:0;color:#d2544e;font-family:var(--font);\n  font-size:12.5px;font-weight:650;cursor:pointer;padding:8px}\n\n.quiz{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radiusLg);\n  padding:18px;margin-bottom:14px;box-shadow:var(--shadow)}\n.qz-top{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;margin-bottom:14px}\n.qz-n{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--muted);flex:1}\n.qz-score{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:750;color:var(--acc);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.qz-q{font-size:18px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.4;margin-bottom:15px}\n.qz-opts{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;margin-bottom:12px}\n.qz-opt{text-align:left;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface2);color:var(--ink);\n  border-radius:13px;padding:13px 14px;font-size:14.5px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;\n  font-family:var(--font);line-height:1.4;transition:.12s}\n.qz-opt:active{transform:scale(.99)}\n.qz-opt.right{border-color:#2f9e5e;background:rgba(47,158,94,.14);color:#2f9e5e}\n.qz-opt.wrong{border-color:#d2544e;background:rgba(210,84,78,.13);color:#d2544e}\n.qz-opt.dim{opacity:.5}\n.quizdone{text-align:center;padding:26px 18px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius:var(--radiusLg);box-shadow:var(--shadow);margin-bottom:14px}\n.quizdone h3{margin:0 0 4px;font-size:19px;font-weight:800}\n.quizdone p{margin:0 0 16px;font-size:13.5px;color:var(--muted)}\n\n.done{text-align:center;padding:26px 18px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius:var(--radiusLg);box-shadow:var(--shadow);margin-bottom:14px}\n.done-emoji{font-size:38px;margin-bottom:6px}\n.done h3{margin:0 0 4px;font-size:17px;font-weight:750}\n.done p{margin:0 0 14px;font-size:13.5px;color:var(--muted)}\n\n.statsrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:8px;margin-bottom:16px}\n.stat{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;padding:11px 8px;\n  text-align:center;box-shadow:var(--shadow)}\n.stat b{display:block;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.02em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.stat span{display:block;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;color:var(--faint);text-transform:uppercase;\n  letter-spacing:.05em;margin-top:2px}\n.stat.hot b{color:var(--acc)}\n\n.deck-s .due{color:var(--acc);font-weight:700}\n.deck-acts{display:flex;gap:2px;flex:0 0 auto;align-items:center}\n.dact{border:0;background:none;color:var(--faint);font-size:14px;cursor:pointer;padding:6px 5px;\n  border-radius:8px;font-family:var(--font);line-height:1}\n.dact:active{background:var(--surface2)}\n.dact.on{color:#e8b422}\n.dact.del.armed{color:#fff;background:#d2544e;font-size:11px;font-weight:750;padding:5px 8px}\n.renamebox{display:flex;gap:7px;margin-top:7px}\n.renamebox input{flex:1;min-width:0;background:var(--surface2);border:1px solid var(--border);\n  color:var(--ink);border-radius:10px;padding:8px 10px;font-family:var(--font);font-size:13.5px}\n.renamebox button{border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:8px 12px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;\n  background:var(--acc);color:#fff;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font)}\n.dots{display:flex;gap:6px;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:0 0 14px}\n.dot{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--border);transition:.2s}\n.dot.on{background:var(--acc);transform:scale(1.35)}\n.nav{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:6px}\n.nav button{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);color:var(--ink);border-radius:12px;\n  padding:11px 18px;font-weight:650;font-size:14px;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--font);transition:transform .1s}\n.nav button:active{transform:scale(.97)}\n.nav .count{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:600}\n\n/* saved decks */\n.section{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);margin:16px 2px 10px}\n.deck{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius:14px;padding:11px 13px;margin-bottom:8px;box-shadow:var(--shadow);cursor:pointer;transition:border-color .2s,background .2s}\n.deck.on{border-color:var(--acc);background:var(--accSoft)}\n.deck-ic{width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:10px;flex:0 0 auto;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:17px;\n  background:var(--surface2);border:1px solid var(--border)}\n.deck.on .deck-ic{background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--acc),var(--acc2));border-color:transparent}\n.deck-mid{flex:1;min-width:0}\n.deck-t{font-size:15px;font-weight:650;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}\n.deck-s{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:1px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px}\n.now{font-size:10px;font-weight:800;color:#fff;background:var(--acc);border-radius:999px;padding:2px 7px;letter-spacing:.03em;text-transform:uppercase}\n.del{border:0;background:none;color:var(--faint);font-size:15px;padding:6px;cursor:pointer;flex:0 0 auto}\n.del:active{color:#ff453a}\n\n.empty{display:none;text-align:center;padding:30px 20px 10px;color:var(--muted)}\n.empty-emoji{font-size:44px;line-height:1}\n.empty h3{margin:12px 0 5px;font-size:17px;color:var(--ink);font-weight:700}\n.empty p{margin:0 auto;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.5;max-width:280px}\n\n@media(prefers-reduced-motion:no-preference){\n  .hero,.surface{animation:rise .45s ease backwards}\n  @keyframes rise{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(9px)}to{opacity:1;transform:none}}\n}\n@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.card-inner{transition:none}}\n</style></head><body>\n<style>\n@keyframes myllmAiSpin{to{transform:rotate(360deg)}}\n.myllm-ai-busy{position:fixed;left:50%;bottom:calc(18px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));transform:translateX(-50%) translateY(18px);z-index:99999;opacity:0;pointer-events:none;transition:opacity .25s,transform .25s;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;background:rgba(28,28,30,.96);color:#fff;border-radius:999px;padding:10px 16px 10px 14px;box-shadow:0 6px 22px rgba(0,0,0,.4);font-family:-apple-system,system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;max-width:92%}\n.myllm-ai-busy.on{opacity:1;transform:translateX(-50%) translateY(0)}\n.myllm-ai-cog{font-size:18px;line-height:1;animation:myllmAiSpin 2.4s linear infinite;filter:drop-shadow(0 0 5px rgba(124,92,255,.85))}\n.myllm-ai-busy small{font-weight:400;opacity:.6}\n</style>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  if(window.__myllmAiWrap||typeof window.myllmAsk!=='function')return;\n  window.__myllmAiWrap=true;\n  var orig=window.myllmAsk,depth=0,node=null;\n  function ensure(){if(node)return;node=document.createElement('div');node.className='myllm-ai-busy';\n    node.innerHTML='<span class=\"myllm-ai-cog\">⚙️</span><span>AI is thinking… <small>privately, on your device</small></span>';\n    (document.body||document.documentElement).appendChild(node);}\n  function show(){ensure();depth++;node.classList.add('on');}\n  function hide(){depth=Math.max(0,depth-1);if(depth===0&&node)node.classList.remove('on');}\n  window.myllmAsk=function(){show();var p;try{p=orig.apply(this,arguments);}catch(e){hide();throw e;}\n    return Promise.resolve(p).then(function(r){hide();return r;},function(e){hide();throw e;});};\n})();\n</script>\n\n<div class=\"hero\">\n  <div class=\"hero-badge\">🧠</div>\n  <div><h1>Flashcard Forge</h1><p>Turn any topic into a study deck in seconds.</p></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"surface\">\n  <div class=\"srcrow\" id=\"srcRow\">\n    <button class=\"src on\" data-src=\"topic\" onclick=\"setSource('topic')\">From a topic</button>\n    <button class=\"src\" data-src=\"notes\" onclick=\"setSource('notes')\">From my notes</button>\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"srcTopic\">\n    <label class=\"field\"><span class=\"field-ic\">✨</span><input id=\"topic\" placeholder=\"Topic — e.g. The Tudors, photosynthesis\"></label>\n    <div class=\"chips\" id=\"topicChips\"></div>\n  </div>\n  <div id=\"srcNotes\" style=\"display:none\">\n    <textarea id=\"notes\" rows=\"6\" placeholder=\"Paste your notes, a lesson, an article — anything you need to revise. Cards are made from this text, not from general knowledge.\"></textarea>\n    <div class=\"notemeta\" id=\"noteMeta\"></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"sizerow\"><span class=\"sizelbl\">Cards</span><div class=\"chips tight\" id=\"sizeChips\"></div></div>\n  <div class=\"sizerow\"><span class=\"sizelbl\">Level</span><div class=\"chips tight\" id=\"levelChips\"></div></div>\n  <button class=\"btn-primary\" id=\"gen\" onclick=\"gen()\">Forge deck 🔨</button>\n  <button class=\"btn-ghost\" style=\"margin:9px 0 0\" onclick=\"newEmptyDeck()\">✍️ Or build a deck by hand</button>\n  <div id=\"status\" class=\"status\"></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"empty\" id=\"empty\">\n  <div class=\"empty-emoji\">🗂️</div>\n  <h3>No decks yet</h3>\n  <p>Type a topic above and your AI tutor forges a study deck to flip through — or build one by hand, a card at a time.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div id=\"study\">\n  <div class=\"deck-head\">\n    <div class=\"badge\">🧠</div>\n    <div style=\"min-width:0\"><div class=\"dt\" id=\"deckTopic\"></div><div class=\"dm\" id=\"deckMeta\"></div></div>\n    <button class=\"headfs\" id=\"fsBtn\" onclick=\"enterFs()\" aria-label=\"Study fullscreen\" title=\"Study fullscreen\">⛶</button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"card\" onclick=\"flip()\">\n    <div class=\"card-inner\" id=\"cardInner\">\n      <div class=\"face front\"><span class=\"face-label\">Question</span><div class=\"face-text\" id=\"qText\"></div><div class=\"face-tip\">tap to flip</div></div>\n      <div class=\"face back\"><span class=\"face-label\">Answer</span><div class=\"face-text\" id=\"aText\"></div><div class=\"face-tip\">tap to flip back</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"grades\" id=\"grades\"></div>\n  <div class=\"dots\" id=\"dots\"></div>\n  <div class=\"nav\">\n    <button onclick=\"nav(-1)\">‹ Prev</button>\n    <span class=\"count\" id=\"count\"></span>\n    <button onclick=\"nav(1)\">Next ›</button>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"tools\">\n    <button class=\"toolsbtn\" id=\"toolsBtn\" onclick=\"toggleTools()\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"toolsBody\">\n      <span>Deck tools</span><span class=\"caret\" id=\"toolsCaret\">▾</span>\n    </button>\n    <div class=\"toolsbody\" id=\"toolsBody\" style=\"display:none\">\n      <div class=\"cardacts\">\n        <button onclick=\"editCard()\">✎ Edit card</button>\n        <button onclick=\"addCard()\">＋ Add card</button>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"cardacts\">\n        <button onclick=\"shuffleQueue()\">🔀 Shuffle</button>\n        <button id=\"revBtn\" onclick=\"toggleReverse()\">⇄ Reverse</button>\n      </div>\n      <button class=\"btn-ghost\" id=\"quizBtn\" onclick=\"startQuiz()\">🎯 Quiz me</button>\n      <button class=\"btn-ghost\" id=\"moreBtn\" onclick=\"forgeMore()\">✨ Forge more cards for this deck</button>\n      <div id=\"moreStatus\" class=\"status\"></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"editor\" id=\"editor\" style=\"display:none\">\n    <div class=\"ed-t\" id=\"edTitle\">Edit card</div>\n    <label class=\"ed-l\" for=\"edQ\">Question</label>\n    <textarea id=\"edQ\" rows=\"3\" placeholder=\"What goes on the front?\"></textarea>\n    <label class=\"ed-l\" for=\"edA\">Answer</label>\n    <textarea id=\"edA\" rows=\"4\" placeholder=\"What goes on the back?\"></textarea>\n    <div class=\"ed-msg\" id=\"edMsg\"></div>\n    <div class=\"ed-row\">\n      <button class=\"btn-ghost\" style=\"margin:0\" onclick=\"closeEditor()\">Cancel</button>\n      <button class=\"btn-primary\" onclick=\"saveEditor()\">Save card</button>\n    </div>\n    <button class=\"btn-ghost\" style=\"margin:9px 0 0\" onclick=\"saveEditor(true)\">Save &amp; add another</button>\n    <button class=\"ed-del\" id=\"edDel\" onclick=\"deleteCard()\">Delete this card</button>\n  </div>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" id=\"quiz\" style=\"display:none\">\n    <div class=\"qz-top\">\n      <span class=\"qz-n\" id=\"qzN\"></span>\n      <span class=\"qz-score\" id=\"qzScore\"></span>\n      <button class=\"fs-x\" onclick=\"endQuiz()\" aria-label=\"Leave quiz\">✕</button>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"qz-q\" id=\"qzQ\"></div>\n    <div class=\"qz-opts\" id=\"qzOpts\"></div>\n    <button class=\"btn-primary\" id=\"qzNext\" style=\"display:none\" onclick=\"quizNext()\">Next question</button>\n  </div>\n\n<div class=\"quizdone\" id=\"quizDone\" style=\"display:none\">\n    <div class=\"done-emoji\" id=\"qdEmoji\">🎯</div>\n    <h3 id=\"qdT\"></h3>\n    <p id=\"qdP\"></p>\n    <button class=\"btn-primary\" onclick=\"startQuiz()\">Play again</button>\n    <button class=\"btn-ghost\" style=\"margin-top:9px\" onclick=\"endQuiz()\">Back to the deck</button>\n  </div>\n\n<div class=\"done\" id=\"done\" style=\"display:none\">\n    <div class=\"done-emoji\">🎉</div>\n    <h3 id=\"doneT\"></h3>\n    <p id=\"doneP\"></p>\n    <button class=\"btn-ghost\" onclick=\"studyAll()\">Study the whole deck again</button>\n  </div>\n\n<div class=\"fs\" id=\"fs\" role=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\" aria-label=\"Fullscreen study\">\n  <div class=\"fs-top\">\n    <span class=\"fs-topic\" id=\"fsTopic\"></span>\n    <span class=\"fs-count\" id=\"fsCount\"></span>\n    <button class=\"fs-x\" onclick=\"exitFs()\" aria-label=\"Leave fullscreen\">✕</button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"fs-bar\"><i id=\"fsBar\"></i></div>\n  <div class=\"fs-stage\" id=\"fsStage\">\n    <div class=\"card-inner\" id=\"fsInner\">\n      <div class=\"face front\"><span class=\"face-label\">Question</span><div class=\"face-text\" id=\"fsQ\"></div><div class=\"face-tip\">tap to flip · swipe to move</div></div>\n      <div class=\"face back\"><span class=\"face-label\">Answer</span><div class=\"face-text\" id=\"fsA\"></div><div class=\"face-tip\">tap to flip back</div></div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"grades\" id=\"fsGrades\"></div>\n  <div class=\"fs-nav\">\n    <button onclick=\"nav(-1)\">‹ Prev</button>\n    <span class=\"fs-hint\" id=\"fsHint\"></span>\n    <button onclick=\"nav(1)\">Next ›</button>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div id=\"savedWrap\" style=\"display:none\">\n  <div class=\"statsrow\" id=\"statsRow\"></div>\n  <div class=\"section\">Saved decks</div>\n  <div id=\"decks\"></div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n\"use strict\";\nvar store=window.myllmStorage||{getItem:function(){return Promise.resolve(null)},setItem:function(){return Promise.resolve()}};\nvar decks=[],cur=-1,idx=0,showA=false;\n/* How many cards to ask for. Small on-device models get less reliable the more\n   you ask for in one go, so the parser takes whatever actually comes back and\n   the status line reports it when it differs from the request — better than\n   silently pretending you got twenty. */\nvar SIZES=[5,8,12,20], deckSize=8;\n/* Level is folded into the generation prompt. One line, but it changes the\n   output more than anything else on this screen. */\nvar LEVELS=[['beginner','Beginner'],['standard','Standard'],['advanced','Advanced'],['expert','Expert']];\nvar level='standard';\n/* Reverse shows the answer first — much harder, and much better for recall\n   than repeatedly recognising a prompt you have already memorised the shape of. */\nvar reverseMode=false;\nvar source='topic';        // 'topic' | 'notes'\nfunction setSource(k){\n  source=k;\n  document.querySelectorAll('#srcRow .src').forEach(function(b){b.classList.toggle('on',b.dataset.src===k)});\n  el('srcTopic').style.display=k==='topic'?'block':'none';\n  el('srcNotes').style.display=k==='notes'?'block':'none';\n  setStatus('');haptic('selection');\n}\n/* Cards built FROM supplied text rather than from the model's own knowledge —\n   which is what makes this useful for the material you are actually sitting an\n   exam on. The instruction is emphatic because small models drift back to\n   general knowledge the moment the passage gets thin. */\nfunction notesPrompt(text,want,lvl){\n  return 'Here is study material:\\n\"\"\"\\n'+text+'\\n\"\"\"\\n\\n'+\n    'Create exactly '+want+' study flashcards USING ONLY the material above. '+\n    'Do not add facts that are not in it. '+lvl+' '+\n    'Reply with EXACTLY these labelled lines and nothing else:\\n'+\n    'CARD: the question on the front | the answer on the back (repeat this line for all '+want+' cards)';\n}\n\n/* ---------------- spaced repetition ----------------\n\n   SM-2, the algorithm Anki is built on. Each card carries its own ease and\n   interval, and a deck opens on what is actually DUE rather than on card one —\n   which is the whole difference between a card viewer and a study app.\n\n   Days are whole-day numbers rather than timestamps. Study at 23:50 and again\n   at 00:10 and you should get the next day's queue, not a card that is\n   technically due in nine hours; whole days match how people think about\n   revision and sidestep timezone drift entirely.\n\n   Cards made before this existed simply have no `srs`, and cardSrs() gives\n   them a fresh one on first touch — so old decks migrate by being used.       */\nfunction today(){ return Math.floor(Date.now()/86400000); }\nfunction cardSrs(c){\n  if(!c.srs)c.srs={ease:2.5,ivl:0,due:0,reps:0,lapses:0};\n  return c.srs;\n}\nfunction isDue(c){ return cardSrs(c).due<=today(); }\nfunction dueCount(deck){\n  var k=0;(deck.cards||[]).forEach(function(c){ if(isDue(c))k++; });\n  return k;\n}\n/* What each button would do, so the choice is informed rather than a guess. */\nfunction previewIvl(s,g){\n  var t=Object.assign({},s);\n  applyGrade(t,g);\n  return g===0?'<1m':(t.ivl===1?'1d':t.ivl+'d');\n}\nfunction applyGrade(s,g){\n  if(g===0){\n    s.lapses++;s.reps=0;s.ivl=0;\n    s.ease=Math.max(1.3,s.ease-0.20);\n    s.due=today();                       // still today: it returns this session\n  }else{\n    if(g===1){ s.ease=Math.max(1.3,s.ease-0.15);\n               s.ivl=s.reps?Math.max(1,Math.round(s.ivl*1.2)):1; }\n    else if(g===2){ s.ivl=s.reps===0?1:(s.reps===1?6:Math.round(s.ivl*s.ease)); }\n    else { s.ease=Math.min(3.0,s.ease+0.15);\n           s.ivl=s.reps===0?4:Math.round(s.ivl*s.ease*1.3); }\n    s.reps++;\n    s.ivl=Math.max(1,s.ivl);\n    s.due=today()+s.ivl;\n  }\n}\n\n/* ---- session queue ----\n   idx indexes the QUEUE, not the deck, so \"next\" means the next card to study\n   rather than the next card in storage. */\nvar queue=[],studyAllMode=false;\nfunction buildQueue(all){\n  var deck=decks[cur];queue=[];\n  if(!deck)return;\n  deck.cards.forEach(function(c,i){ if(all||isDue(c))queue.push(i); });\n  if(!queue.length&&!all)studyAllMode=false;   // nothing due -> the done card shows\n  idx=0;showA=false;\n}\nfunction studyAll(){\n  studyAllMode=true;buildQueue(true);\n  el('done').style.display='none';\n  renderCard();haptic('light');\n}\nfunction curCard(){\n  var deck=decks[cur];\n  if(!deck||!queue.length)return null;\n  return deck.cards[queue[Math.min(idx,queue.length-1)]];\n}\nfunction grade(g){\n  var deck=decks[cur];if(!deck||!queue.length)return;\n  var ci=queue[idx],c=deck.cards[ci];\n  applyGrade(cardSrs(c),g);\n  bumpStats(g>=2);\n  if(g===0){\n    // put it back a few cards on rather than at the end, so a card you just\n    // failed is retried while it is still fresh\n    queue.splice(idx,1);\n    queue.splice(Math.min(queue.length,idx+3),0,ci);\n  }else{\n    queue.splice(idx,1);\n    if(idx>=queue.length)idx=queue.length?queue.length-1:0;\n  }\n  showA=false;save();\n  renderDecks();                      // the \"N due\" counts are live, not stale\n  if(!queue.length){ finishSession(); return; }\n  renderCard();haptic('selection');\n}\nfunction finishSession(){\n  el('study').style.display='none';\n  el('done').style.display='block';\n  renderDecks();\n  var deck=decks[cur];\n  var soon=deck?deck.cards.reduce(function(m,c){\n    var d=cardSrs(c).due;return (m===null||d<m)?d:m; },null):null;\n  el('doneT').textContent='Deck complete';\n  el('doneP').textContent = soon!==null\n    ? (soon<=today()?'Everything reviewed for now.'\n       :'Next cards are due in '+(soon-today())+' day'+((soon-today())===1?'':'s')+'.')\n    : 'Everything reviewed.';\n  haptic('success');\n}\n\n/* Extend a deck instead of starting over. The existing questions go into the\n   prompt so the model adds rather than repeats — the same trick that stopped\n   Social Studio's week series producing five variations of one post. */\nfunction forgeMore(){\n  var deck=decks[cur];if(!deck)return;\n  var msg=el('moreStatus');msg.textContent='';\n  if(!window.myllmAsk){msg.textContent='This needs AI access — enable it in MyLLM Settings.';return}\n  var want=deckSize;\n  var have=deck.cards.map(function(c){return c.q}).slice(0,40);\n  el('moreBtn').disabled=true;msg.textContent='Forging '+want+' more…';\n  var lvl={beginner:'Pitch them for a complete beginner.',standard:'Pitch them at a general adult learner.',\n           advanced:'Pitch them at an advanced student.',expert:'Pitch them at an expert.'}[level];\n  var p='Create exactly '+want+' MORE study flashcards about: '+deck.topic+'. '+lvl+'\\n'+\n    'These questions are already covered — do NOT repeat them or ask the same thing differently:\\n'+\n    have.map(function(q){return '- '+q}).join('\\n')+'\\n'+\n    'Reply with EXACTLY these labelled lines and nothing else:\\n'+\n    'CARD: the question on the front | the answer on the back (repeat this line for all '+want+' cards)';\n  myllmAsk(p).then(function(r){return parseDeck(r||'')})\n  .then(function(cards){\n    // a model that ignores the exclusion list would silently bloat the deck\n    var seen={};deck.cards.forEach(function(c){seen[c.q.toLowerCase().trim()]=1});\n    var fresh=cards.filter(function(c){return !seen[c.q.toLowerCase().trim()]});\n    if(!fresh.length)throw new Error('every suggestion repeated a card you already have');\n    fresh.forEach(function(c){cardSrs(c);deck.cards.push(c);queue.push(deck.cards.length-1)});\n    save();renderDecks();renderCard();\n    msg.textContent='Added '+fresh.length+' card'+(fresh.length===1?'':'s')+\n      (fresh.length<cards.length\n        ? (function(d){return ' — '+d+(d===1?' was a duplicate and was':' were duplicates and were')+' dropped.'})(cards.length-fresh.length)\n        : '.');\n    haptic('success');\n  })\n  .catch(function(e){msg.textContent='Could not add cards: '+e.message})\n  .then(function(){el('moreBtn').disabled=false});\n}\n\n/* ---------------- quiz ----------------\n\n   Recognition rather than recall — a different, easier cognitive mode than\n   flipping, which is exactly why it is a separate button and not a replacement\n   for it. Distractors come from other answers in the SAME deck, so they are\n   plausible; drawing them from elsewhere would make every question trivial.\n\n   Grading here feeds the same SM-2 schedule: getting a card right in a quiz is\n   evidence you know it, and pretending otherwise would make the two modes\n   disagree about the same card.                                               */\nvar quiz=null;\nfunction startQuiz(){\n  var deck=decks[cur];if(!deck)return;\n  if(deck.cards.length<4){\n    el('moreStatus').textContent='A quiz needs at least 4 cards — forge a few more first.';\n    return;\n  }\n  var order=deck.cards.map(function(_,i){return i});\n  for(var i=order.length-1;i>0;i--){var j=Math.floor(Math.random()*(i+1)),t=order[i];order[i]=order[j];order[j]=t}\n  quiz={order:order.slice(0,Math.min(10,order.length)),pos:0,score:0,answered:false};\n  el('study').style.display='none';el('done').style.display='none';\n  el('quizDone').style.display='none';el('quiz').style.display='block';\n  renderQuiz();haptic('light');\n}\nfunction endQuiz(){\n  quiz=null;\n  el('quiz').style.display='none';el('quizDone').style.display='none';\n  if(queue.length){el('study').style.display='block';renderCard()}\n  else finishSession();\n}\nfunction renderQuiz(){\n  var deck=decks[cur];if(!deck||!quiz)return;\n  var ci=quiz.order[quiz.pos],card=deck.cards[ci];\n  el('qzN').textContent='Question '+(quiz.pos+1)+' of '+quiz.order.length;\n  el('qzScore').textContent=quiz.score+' correct';\n  el('qzQ').textContent=card.q;\n  // three wrong answers from elsewhere in this deck, deduped by text so a\n  // repeated answer can never appear as two different options\n  var pool=[],seen={};seen[card.a.trim().toLowerCase()]=1;\n  deck.cards.forEach(function(c,i){\n    if(i===ci)return;\n    var k=c.a.trim().toLowerCase();\n    if(seen[k])return;seen[k]=1;pool.push(c.a);\n  });\n  for(var i=pool.length-1;i>0;i--){var j=Math.floor(Math.random()*(i+1)),t=pool[i];pool[i]=pool[j];pool[j]=t}\n  var opts=pool.slice(0,3).concat([card.a]);\n  for(var k2=opts.length-1;k2>0;k2--){var j2=Math.floor(Math.random()*(k2+1)),t2=opts[k2];opts[k2]=opts[j2];opts[j2]=t2}\n  var box=el('qzOpts');box.innerHTML='';\n  quiz.answered=false;\n  opts.forEach(function(o){\n    var b=document.createElement('button');b.className='qz-opt';b.type='button';b.textContent=o;\n    b.onclick=function(){ answerQuiz(b,o===card.a,ci) };\n    box.appendChild(b);\n  });\n  el('qzNext').style.display='none';\n}\nfunction answerQuiz(btn,right,ci){\n  if(!quiz||quiz.answered)return;\n  quiz.answered=true;\n  var deck=decks[cur],card=deck.cards[ci];\n  [].forEach.call(el('qzOpts').children,function(b){\n    if(b.textContent===card.a)b.classList.add('right');\n    else if(b===btn)b.classList.add('wrong');\n    else b.classList.add('dim');\n  });\n  if(right)quiz.score++;\n  // a quiz answer is real evidence, so it moves the same schedule\n  applyGrade(cardSrs(card),right?2:0);\n  bumpStats(right);\n  save();renderDecks();\n  el('qzNext').style.display='block';\n  el('qzScore').textContent=quiz.score+' correct';\n  haptic(right?'success':'warning');\n}\nfunction quizNext(){\n  if(!quiz)return;\n  quiz.pos++;\n  if(quiz.pos>=quiz.order.length){ finishQuiz(); return; }\n  renderQuiz();\n}\nfunction finishQuiz(){\n  var n=quiz.order.length,sc=quiz.score,pct=Math.round(sc/n*100);\n  el('quiz').style.display='none';el('quizDone').style.display='block';\n  el('qdEmoji').textContent=pct===100?'🏆':pct>=70?'🎉':pct>=40?'👍':'📚';\n  el('qdT').textContent=sc+' out of '+n;\n  el('qdP').textContent=pct===100?'Perfect round.'\n    :pct>=70?'Solid — the ones you missed are back in the deck sooner.'\n    :'The misses are scheduled to come round again quickly.';\n  quiz=null;haptic('success');\n}\n\n/* ---------------- editing ----------------\n\n   A deck used to be whatever the model said, permanently — one wrong answer\n   and the only remedy was regenerating the lot. Editing preserves the card's\n   schedule: fixing a typo should not reset how well you know it.             */\nvar editingIdx=-2;                       // -2 closed, -1 new card, >=0 deck index\nfunction openEditor(deckIdx){\n  var deck=decks[cur];if(!deck)return;\n  editingIdx=deckIdx;\n  var c=deckIdx>=0?deck.cards[deckIdx]:{q:'',a:''};\n  el('edQ').value=c.q||'';\n  el('edA').value=c.a||'';\n  el('edMsg').textContent='';\n  el('edTitle').textContent=deckIdx>=0?'Edit card':'New card';\n  el('edDel').style.display=(deckIdx>=0&&deck.cards.length>1)?'block':'none';\n  el('editor').style.display='block';\n  el('study').style.display='none';\n  el('edQ').focus();\n}\nfunction editCard(){\n  if(cur<0||!queue.length)return;\n  openEditor(queue[idx]);\n}\nfunction addCard(){ if(cur>=0)openEditor(-1); }\n/* Every deck used to come from the model, so with AI off — or simply\n   unavailable — the app had no way to make a deck at all. Writing your own\n   cards is a legitimate way to study, not a fallback. */\nfunction newEmptyDeck(){\n  var name=el('topic').value.trim()||'My deck';\n  decks.unshift({topic:name,cards:[]});\n  sortDecks();save();\n  el('topic').value='';setStatus('');\n  cur=decks.indexOf(decks.find(function(d){return d.topic===name&&!d.cards.length}));\n  if(cur<0)cur=0;\n  queue=[];idx=0;showA=false;studyAllMode=false;\n  renderDecks();updateViews();\n  el('done').style.display='none';\n  openEditor(-1);\n  haptic('success');\n}\nfunction closeEditor(){\n  editingIdx=-2;\n  el('editor').style.display='none';\n  var deck=decks[cur];\n  if(deck&&!deck.cards.length){\n    // an empty deck has nothing to finish — drop it rather than leave a husk\n    decks.splice(cur,1);cur=-1;save();\n    el('study').style.display='none';renderDecks();updateViews();\n    return;\n  }\n  if(queue.length){ el('study').style.display='block'; renderCard(); }\n  else finishSession();\n}\n/* Building a deck by hand means writing card after card, so the flow stays in\n   the editor rather than bouncing out to a drawer for every one. */\nfunction saveEditor(again){\n  var deck=decks[cur];if(!deck)return;\n  var q=el('edQ').value.trim(),a=el('edA').value.trim();\n  if(!q||!a){ el('edMsg').textContent='Both sides need something on them.'; return; }\n  if(editingIdx>=0){\n    // keep the existing srs — a wording fix is not a reason to forget the card\n    deck.cards[editingIdx].q=q;\n    deck.cards[editingIdx].a=a;\n  }else{\n    var card={q:q,a:a};cardSrs(card);\n    deck.cards.push(card);\n    queue.push(deck.cards.length-1);      // study it in this session\n    if(queue.length===1)idx=0;\n  }\n  save();renderDecks();haptic('success');\n  if(again===true){\n    editingIdx=-1;\n    el('edQ').value='';el('edA').value='';el('edMsg').textContent='';\n    el('edTitle').textContent='New card';\n    el('edDel').style.display='none';\n    el('edQ').focus();\n    return;\n  }\n  closeEditor();\n}\nfunction deleteCard(){\n  var deck=decks[cur];if(!deck||editingIdx<0||deck.cards.length<2)return;\n  var gone=editingIdx;\n  deck.cards.splice(gone,1);\n  // queue holds DECK indices, so every entry past the hole shifts down by one\n  queue=queue.filter(function(i){return i!==gone;})\n             .map(function(i){return i>gone?i-1:i;});\n  if(idx>=queue.length)idx=queue.length?queue.length-1:0;\n  save();editingIdx=-2;\n  el('editor').style.display='none';\n  renderDecks();\n  if(queue.length){ el('study').style.display='block'; showA=false; renderCard(); }\n  else finishSession();\n  haptic('warning');\n}\n\n/* Reviews and a day streak, kept here so the stats view has data to show. */\nvar stats={reviews:0,correct:0,day:0,streak:0};\nfunction bumpStats(right){\n  var t=today();\n  if(stats.day!==t){ stats.streak=(stats.day===t-1)?stats.streak+1:1; stats.day=t; }\n  stats.reviews++;\n  if(right)stats.correct++;\n  store.setItem('stats',JSON.stringify(stats));\n}\nfunction el(i){return document.getElementById(i)}\nfunction setStatus(t){el('status').textContent=t}\nfunction save(){store.setItem('decks',JSON.stringify(decks))}\nfunction haptic(k){if(window.myllmHaptic)try{myllmHaptic(k)}catch(e){}}\n\nvar EXAMPLES=['The Tudors','Photosynthesis','French verbs','World capitals','Music theory'];\nfunction buildSizes(){\n  var c=el('sizeChips');if(!c)return;\n  c.innerHTML='';\n  SIZES.forEach(function(nn){\n    var b=document.createElement('button');b.type='button';\n    b.className='chip'+(nn===deckSize?' on':'');b.textContent=nn;\n    b.onclick=function(){deckSize=nn;buildSizes();store.setItem('decksize',String(nn));haptic('selection')};\n    c.appendChild(b);\n  });\n}\nfunction buildLevels(){\n  var c=el('levelChips');if(!c)return;\n  c.innerHTML='';\n  LEVELS.forEach(function(o){\n    var b=document.createElement('button');b.type='button';\n    b.className='chip'+(o[0]===level?' on':'');b.textContent=o[1];\n    b.onclick=function(){level=o[0];buildLevels();store.setItem('level',o[0]);haptic('selection')};\n    c.appendChild(b);\n  });\n}\n/* Fisher-Yates over the QUEUE, not the deck: shuffling storage would scramble\n   what \"card 4\" means for every other view. */\nfunction shuffleQueue(){\n  for(var i=queue.length-1;i>0;i--){\n    var j=Math.floor(Math.random()*(i+1)),t=queue[i];queue[i]=queue[j];queue[j]=t;\n  }\n  idx=0;showA=false;renderCard();haptic('success');\n}\nvar toolsOpen=false;\nfunction applyTools(){\n  var body=el('toolsBody'),btn=el('toolsBtn');\n  if(!body||!btn)return;\n  body.style.display=toolsOpen?'block':'none';\n  btn.classList.toggle('open',toolsOpen);\n  btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded',toolsOpen?'true':'false');\n}\nfunction toggleTools(){\n  toolsOpen=!toolsOpen;\n  applyTools();\n  store.setItem('tools',toolsOpen?'1':'0');\n  haptic('selection');\n}\nfunction toggleReverse(){\n  reverseMode=!reverseMode;\n  store.setItem('reverse',reverseMode?'1':'0');\n  showA=false;renderCard();haptic('selection');\n}\nfunction buildChips(){\n  var c=el('topicChips');c.innerHTML='';\n  EXAMPLES.forEach(function(t){\n    var b=document.createElement('button');b.type='button';b.className='chip';b.textContent=t;\n    b.onclick=function(){el('topic').value=t;\n      document.querySelectorAll('.chip').forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});\n      b.classList.add('on');haptic('selection');};\n    c.appendChild(b);\n  });\n}\n\n/* Labelled lines, not JSON — small models (Apple Intelligence) echo JSON\n   templates back verbatim. Echoed instructions are rejected and retried. */\nvar ECHO=/question on the front|answer on the back|repeat this line|labelled line/i;\nfunction parseDeck(reply){\n  var cards=[],got=false;\n  String(reply||'').split(/\\r?\\n/).forEach(function(raw){\n    var ln=raw.replace(/\\*\\*/g,'').trim();\n    var m=ln.match(/^[-*#>\\s]*(CARDS?)\\s*\\d*\\s*[:：]\\s*(.*)$/i);\n    if(!m)return;\n    got=true;\n    var parts=m[2].split('|');\n    var q=(parts[0]||'').trim(),a=parts.slice(1).join('|').trim();\n    if(q&&a)cards.push({q:q,a:a});\n  });\n  if(!got){ // model answered in the old JSON shape — accept it\n    var s=String(reply||'').indexOf('['),e=String(reply||'').lastIndexOf(']');\n    if(s>=0&&e>s)try{\n      var j=JSON.parse(String(reply).slice(s,e+1));\n      if(Array.isArray(j))j.forEach(function(c){if(c&&c.q&&c.a)cards.push({q:String(c.q),a:String(c.a)})});\n    }catch(e2){}\n  }\n  cards=cards.filter(function(c){return !ECHO.test(c.q)&&!ECHO.test(c.a)});\n  if(!cards.length)throw new Error('the model did not return a deck');\n  return cards;\n}\nfunction gen(){\n  var notes=el('notes')?el('notes').value.trim():'';\n  var topic=el('topic').value.trim();\n  if(source==='notes'){\n    if(notes.length<80){setStatus('Paste a bit more text — at least a paragraph or two to draw cards from.');return}\n  }else if(!topic){setStatus('Enter a topic first.');return}\n  if(!window.myllmAsk){setStatus('This app needs AI access — update MyLLM and enable “Allow apps to use the AI” in Settings.');return}\n  el('gen').disabled=true;\n  setStatus(source==='notes'?'Reading your notes…':'Forging a deck about “'+topic+'”…');\n  var want=deckSize;\n  var lvl={beginner:'Pitch them for a complete beginner — plain words, no jargon.',\n           standard:'Pitch them at a general adult learner.',\n           advanced:'Pitch them at an advanced student who already knows the basics.',\n           expert:'Pitch them at an expert — precise terminology and specifics.'}[level];\n  // Long notes are trimmed: an on-device context window is small, and a\n  // truncated passage yields better cards than an overflowing one yields none.\n  var body=notes.slice(0,4000);\n  var p=source==='notes'\n    ? notesPrompt(body,want,lvl)\n    : 'Create exactly '+want+' study flashcards about: '+topic+'. '+lvl+' Reply with EXACTLY these labelled lines and nothing else:\\n'+\n      'CARD: the question on the front | the answer on the back (repeat this line for all '+want+' cards)';\n  myllmAsk(p).then(function(r){return parseDeck(r||'')})\n  .catch(function(){return myllmAsk(p+'\\nIMPORTANT: fill each labelled line with real content — never repeat the instruction text.')\n    .then(function(r){return parseDeck(r||'')})})\n  .then(function(cards){\n    if(cards.length>want)cards=cards.slice(0,want);\n    var name=source==='notes'\n      ? (body.split(/\\s+/).slice(0,5).join(' ').replace(/[^\\w\\s-]/g,'')||'My notes')\n      : topic;\n    cards.forEach(cardSrs);\n    decks.unshift({topic:name,cards:cards});sortDecks();save();\n    el('topic').value='';cur=-1;openDeck(0);haptic('success');\n    setStatus(cards.length<want\n      ? ('Forged '+cards.length+' cards — the model ran out before '+want+'. Try a smaller deck for a fuller set.')\n      : '');\n  }).catch(function(err){setStatus('Could not generate: '+err.message)})\n  .then(function(){el('gen').disabled=false});\n}\n\nfunction openDeck(i){\n  if(!decks[i]){el('study').style.display='none';if(fsOn)exitFs();return}\n  cur=i;showA=false;studyAllMode=false;\n  el('done').style.display='none';\n  if(!decks[i].cards.length){        // brand new hand-built deck\n    queue=[];renderDecks();updateViews();openEditor(-1);return;\n  }\n  buildQueue(false);\n  if(!queue.length){ renderDecks();updateViews();finishSession();return; }\n  renderCard();renderDecks();updateViews();\n  window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'});\n}\nfunction flip(){\n  showA=!showA;haptic('light');\n  el('cardInner').classList.toggle('flipped',showA);\n  el('fsInner').classList.toggle('flipped',showA);\n  el('fsHint').textContent=showA?'':'tap to reveal';   // flip() bypasses renderCard\n  renderGrades();\n}\n\n/* ---- fullscreen study ---- */\nvar fsOn=false;\nfunction enterFs(){\n  if(cur<0||!decks[cur])return;\n  fsOn=true;\n  el('fs').classList.add('on');\n  document.body.classList.add('fs-open');\n  // real fullscreen where it exists (desktop); harmless no-op on iOS\n  try{ var r=document.documentElement.requestFullscreen; if(r)r.call(document.documentElement).catch(function(){}); }catch(e){}\n  renderCard();haptic('light');\n}\nfunction exitFs(){\n  fsOn=false;\n  el('fs').classList.remove('on');\n  document.body.classList.remove('fs-open');\n  try{ if(document.fullscreenElement&&document.exitFullscreen)document.exitFullscreen().catch(function(){}); }catch(e){}\n  haptic('light');\n}\n/* Swipe to move, tap to flip. The threshold keeps a slightly untidy tap from\n   skipping a card, which is worse than a swipe that fails to register. */\n(function(){\n  var st=el('fsStage'),x0=null,y0=null,moved=false;\n  if(!st)return;\n  st.addEventListener('pointerdown',function(e){x0=e.clientX;y0=e.clientY;moved=false});\n  st.addEventListener('pointermove',function(e){\n    if(x0===null)return;\n    if(Math.abs(e.clientX-x0)>10||Math.abs(e.clientY-y0)>10)moved=true;\n  });\n  st.addEventListener('pointerup',function(e){\n    if(x0===null)return;\n    var dx=e.clientX-x0,dy=e.clientY-y0;\n    x0=null;\n    if(Math.abs(dx)>44&&Math.abs(dx)>Math.abs(dy)){ nav(dx<0?1:-1); return; }\n    if(!moved)flip();\n  });\n  st.addEventListener('pointercancel',function(){x0=null});\n})();\n/* Study shortcuts, with two guards that both have to hold.\n\n   The first is what a field IS: checking only for INPUT missed every TEXTAREA,\n   so typing a space in the card editor flipped the card and typing an \"f\"\n   threw you into fullscreen. Anything a person can type into has to count,\n   including contenteditable and select.\n\n   The second is what is on SCREEN: the shortcuts belong to the study view, so\n   they must not fire while the editor, the quiz or the completion card has the\n   stage — otherwise space flips a card nobody can see. */\nfunction isTyping(){\n  var a=document.activeElement;\n  if(!a)return false;\n  var t=(a.tagName||'').toUpperCase();\n  return t==='INPUT'||t==='TEXTAREA'||t==='SELECT'||a.isContentEditable===true;\n}\nfunction studyVisible(){\n  var e2=el('study');\n  return !!e2&&e2.offsetParent!==null;\n}\ndocument.addEventListener('keydown',function(e){\n  if(e.key==='Escape'&&fsOn){exitFs();return}\n  if(isTyping())return;\n  if(cur<0||!decks[cur])return;\n  if(!fsOn&&!studyVisible())return;\n  if(e.key==='ArrowRight')nav(1);\n  else if(e.key==='ArrowLeft')nav(-1);\n  else if(e.key===' '||e.key==='Enter'){e.preventDefault();flip()}\n  else if((e.key==='f'||e.key==='F')&&!fsOn)enterFs();\n});\nfunction nav(d){\n  if(cur<0||!decks[cur]||!queue.length)return;\n  var n=queue.length;idx=(idx+d+n)%n;showA=false;\n  renderCard();haptic('selection');\n}\nfunction renderCard(){\n  if(cur<0||!decks[cur]){el('study').style.display='none';if(fsOn)exitFs();return}\n  var deck=decks[cur],c=curCard();\n  if(!c){el('study').style.display='none';return}\n  el('study').style.display='block';\n  el('done').style.display='none';\n  el('deckTopic').textContent=deck.topic;\n  var due=dueCount(deck);\n  el('deckMeta').textContent = studyAllMode\n    ? (deck.cards.length+' cards · reviewing all')\n    : (due+' due of '+deck.cards.length+' · tap the card to flip');\n  var front=reverseMode?c.a:c.q, back=reverseMode?c.q:c.a;\n  var fLabel=reverseMode?'Answer':'Question', bLabel=reverseMode?'Question':'Answer';\n  el('qText').textContent=front;\n  el('aText').textContent=back;\n  document.querySelectorAll('.face.front .face-label').forEach(function(e){e.textContent=fLabel});\n  document.querySelectorAll('.face.back .face-label').forEach(function(e){e.textContent=bLabel});\n  var rb=el('revBtn');if(rb)rb.classList.toggle('on',reverseMode);\n  el('cardInner').classList.toggle('flipped',showA);\n  el('count').textContent='Card '+(idx+1)+' of '+queue.length;\n  // the fullscreen layer is a second view of the same card, not a second model\n  el('fsQ').textContent=front;\n  el('fsA').textContent=back;\n  el('fsInner').classList.toggle('flipped',showA);\n  el('fsTopic').textContent=deck.topic;\n  el('fsCount').textContent=(idx+1)+' / '+queue.length;\n  el('fsBar').style.width=(((idx+1)/Math.max(1,queue.length))*100).toFixed(1)+'%';\n  el('fsHint').textContent=showA?'':'tap to reveal';\n  var dd=el('dots');dd.innerHTML='';\n  if(queue.length<=16){\n    queue.forEach(function(_,j){var s=document.createElement('span');s.className='dot'+(j===idx?' on':'');dd.appendChild(s)});\n  }\n  renderGrades();\n}\n\n/* Both views share one grading row builder; the buttons carry the interval\n   each choice would set, so you are picking an outcome, not a mood. */\nfunction renderGrades(){\n  var c=curCard();\n  [['grades'],['fsGrades']].forEach(function(o){\n    var g=el(o[0]);if(!g)return;\n    g.className='grades'+(showA&&c?' on':'');\n    if(!showA||!c){g.innerHTML='';return}\n    var s0=cardSrs(c);\n    g.innerHTML=[[0,'Again'],[1,'Hard'],[2,'Good'],[3,'Easy']].map(function(b){\n      return '<button class=\"grade g'+b[0]+'\" onclick=\"grade('+b[0]+')\">'+\n             '<b>'+b[1]+'</b><span>'+previewIvl(s0,b[0])+'</span></button>';\n    }).join('');\n  });\n}\n\nvar deckArmed=null, renaming=-1;\n/* Starred decks float to the top; everything else keeps its existing order,\n   so pinning never silently reshuffles the rest. */\nfunction sortDecks(){\n  var keep=decks[cur];\n  decks=decks.map(function(d,i){return {d:d,i:i}})\n    .sort(function(a,b){ return (b.d.star?1:0)-(a.d.star?1:0) || a.i-b.i; })\n    .map(function(o){return o.d});\n  if(keep)cur=decks.indexOf(keep);\n}\nfunction startRename(i){ renaming=i;renderDecks(); }\nfunction commitRename(i){\n  var inp=el('rn'+i);if(!inp)return;\n  var v=inp.value.trim();\n  if(v)decks[i].topic=v.slice(0,60);\n  renaming=-1;save();renderDecks();\n  if(i===cur)renderCard();\n  haptic('success');\n}\n/* Anki and Quizlet both import plain CSV, so a shared deck is portable rather\n   than locked in here. Quotes are doubled per RFC 4180. */\nfunction deckCsv(d){\n  function esc(t){ return '\"'+String(t||'').replace(/\"/g,'\"\"')+'\"'; }\n  return d.cards.map(function(c){ return esc(c.q)+','+esc(c.a); }).join('\\r\\n');\n}\n/* UTF-8 -> base64, written out rather than reached for via the usual\n   btoa(unescape(encodeURIComponent(x))) idiom. unescape is deprecated, and it\n   trips scan_app.py's obfuscation heuristic — which is a fair rule, since\n   atob/unescape/fromCharCode really are how hidden payloads get reconstituted.\n   Better to encode explicitly than to teach the reviewer to wave that flag\n   through. The native bridge requires real base64: it strips to \"base64,\" and\n   hands the rest to Data(base64Encoded:), so a percent-encoded data URL fails. */\nvar B64A='ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/';\nfunction b64utf8(str){\n  var bytes=new TextEncoder().encode(str),out='',i=0,n;\n  for(;i+2<bytes.length;i+=3){\n    n=(bytes[i]<<16)|(bytes[i+1]<<8)|bytes[i+2];\n    out+=B64A[(n>>18)&63]+B64A[(n>>12)&63]+B64A[(n>>6)&63]+B64A[n&63];\n  }\n  var rem=bytes.length-i;\n  if(rem===1){ n=bytes[i]<<16; out+=B64A[(n>>18)&63]+B64A[(n>>12)&63]+'=='; }\n  else if(rem===2){ n=(bytes[i]<<16)|(bytes[i+1]<<8);\n    out+=B64A[(n>>18)&63]+B64A[(n>>12)&63]+B64A[(n>>6)&63]+'='; }\n  return out;\n}\nfunction shareDeck(i){\n  var d=decks[i];if(!d)return;\n  var csv=deckCsv(d);\n  if(window.myllmShareFile){\n    var b64;\n    try{ b64='data:text/csv;base64,'+b64utf8(csv); }catch(e){ b64=null; }\n    if(b64){\n      myllmShareFile(b64,{filename:d.topic.replace(/[^\\w -]/g,'').slice(0,40)+'.csv',mime:'text/csv'})\n        .catch(function(){});\n      haptic('success');return;\n    }\n  }\n  var txt=d.topic+'\\n\\n'+d.cards.map(function(c){return c.q+'\\n— '+c.a}).join('\\n\\n');\n  if(window.myllmShare){ try{ myllmShare(txt);haptic('success');return; }catch(e){} }\n  try{\n    var ta=document.createElement('textarea');ta.value=txt;document.body.appendChild(ta);\n    ta.select();document.execCommand('copy');document.body.removeChild(ta);\n    setStatus('Deck copied to the clipboard.');\n  }catch(e){ setStatus('Sharing is not available here.'); }\n}\n\nfunction renderDecks(){\n  var D=el('decks');D.innerHTML='';\n  decks.forEach(function(d,i){\n    var active=(i===cur);\n    var r=document.createElement('div');r.className='deck'+(active?' on':'');\n    var ic=document.createElement('div');ic.className='deck-ic';ic.textContent=active?'📖':'🗂️';\n    var mid=document.createElement('div');mid.className='deck-mid';\n    var t=document.createElement('div');t.className='deck-t';t.textContent=d.topic;\n    var s=document.createElement('div');s.className='deck-s';\n    var dn=dueCount(d);\n    s.innerHTML=(active?'<span class=\"now\">Studying</span>':'')+\n      '<span>'+d.cards.length+' cards</span>'+\n      (dn?'<span class=\"due\">'+dn+' due</span>':'<span>up to date</span>');\n    mid.appendChild(t);mid.appendChild(s);\n    if(renaming===i){\n      t.style.display='none';\n      var rb=document.createElement('div');rb.className='renamebox';\n      var inp=document.createElement('input');inp.id='rn'+i;inp.value=d.topic;inp.maxLength=60;\n      inp.onclick=function(ev){ev.stopPropagation()};\n      inp.onkeydown=function(ev){if(ev.key==='Enter')commitRename(i);if(ev.key==='Escape'){renaming=-1;renderDecks()}};\n      var ok=document.createElement('button');ok.textContent='Save';\n      ok.onclick=function(ev){ev.stopPropagation();commitRename(i)};\n      rb.appendChild(inp);rb.appendChild(ok);\n      mid.appendChild(rb);\n      setTimeout(function(){var e2=el('rn'+i);if(e2){e2.focus();e2.select()}},0);\n    }\n    var acts=document.createElement('div');acts.className='deck-acts';\n    function act(label,aria,fn){\n      var b=document.createElement('button');b.type='button';b.className='dact';\n      b.textContent=label;b.setAttribute('aria-label',aria);\n      b.onclick=function(ev){ev.stopPropagation();fn()};\n      acts.appendChild(b);return b;\n    }\n    var starBtn=act(d.star?'★':'☆','Pin deck to top',function(){\n      d.star=!d.star;sortDecks();save();renderDecks();haptic('selection');\n    });\n    if(d.star)starBtn.classList.add('on');\n    act('✎','Rename deck',function(){ startRename(i) });\n    act('⤴','Share deck',function(){ shareDeck(i) });\n    var x=act(deckArmed===i?'Delete?':'✕','Delete deck',function(){\n      if(deckArmed!==i){\n        deckArmed=i;renderDecks();\n        setTimeout(function(){if(deckArmed===i){deckArmed=null;renderDecks()}},2500);\n        return;\n      }\n      deckArmed=null;\n      decks.splice(i,1);\n      if(cur===i)cur=-1;else if(cur>i)cur--;\n      save();\n      if(decks.length){openDeck(cur<0?0:cur)}else{cur=-1;el('study').style.display='none';renderDecks();updateViews()}\n      haptic('warning');\n    });\n    x.classList.add('del');\n    if(deckArmed===i)x.classList.add('armed');\n    r.appendChild(ic);r.appendChild(mid);r.appendChild(acts);\n    r.onclick=function(){openDeck(i)};\n    D.appendChild(r);\n  });\n  updateViews();\n}\n\n/* Four numbers, no chart. Accuracy is only shown once there is enough of a\n   sample to mean anything — a 100% badge off two reviews flatters nobody. */\nfunction renderStats(){\n  var row=el('statsRow');if(!row)return;\n  var dueAll=decks.reduce(function(k,d){return k+dueCount(d)},0);\n  var cards=decks.reduce(function(k,d){return k+d.cards.length},0);\n  var acc=stats.reviews>=10?Math.round(stats.correct/stats.reviews*100)+'%':'—';\n  var streak=(stats.day===today()||stats.day===today()-1)?stats.streak:0;\n  row.innerHTML=\n    '<div class=\"stat'+(dueAll?' hot':'')+'\"><b>'+dueAll+'</b><span>Due now</span></div>'+\n    '<div class=\"stat\"><b>'+cards+'</b><span>Cards</span></div>'+\n    '<div class=\"stat\"><b>'+stats.reviews+'</b><span>Reviews</span></div>'+\n    '<div class=\"stat\"><b>'+(streak?streak+'d':acc)+'</b><span>'+(streak?'Streak':'Accuracy')+'</span></div>';\n}\n\nfunction updateViews(){\n  el('empty').style.display=decks.length?'none':'block';\n  el('savedWrap').style.display=decks.length?'block':'none';\n  if(!decks.length)el('study').style.display='none';\n  renderStats();\n}\n\nel('topic').addEventListener('keydown',function(e){if(e.key==='Enter')gen()});\nel('notes').addEventListener('input',function(){\n  var v=this.value.trim();\n  el('noteMeta').textContent=v?(v.split(/\\s+/).length+' words'+(v.length>4000?' · only the first 4000 characters are used':'')):'';\n});\n\nbuildChips();buildSizes();buildLevels();\nstore.getItem('tools').then(function(v){\n  toolsOpen=(v==='1');applyTools();\n  return store.getItem('level');\n}).then(function(v){\n  if(v&&LEVELS.some(function(l){return l[0]===v}))level=v;\n  buildLevels();\n  return store.getItem('reverse');\n}).then(function(v){\n  reverseMode=(v==='1');\n  return store.getItem('stats');\n}).then(function(v){\n  if(v)try{var t=JSON.parse(v);if(t&&typeof t==='object')stats=Object.assign(stats,t)}catch(e){}\n  return store.getItem('decksize');\n}).then(function(v){\n  var nn=parseInt(v,10);\n  if(SIZES.indexOf(nn)>=0)deckSize=nn;\n  buildSizes();\n  return store.getItem('decks');\n}).then(function(v){\n  if(v)try{decks=JSON.parse(v)||[]}catch(e){}\n  sortDecks();renderDecks();\n  if(decks.length)openDeck(0);else updateViews();\n  if(!window.myllmAsk)setStatus('Heads-up: this app needs the latest MyLLM with apps-AI enabled.');\n});\n</script></body></html>\n", "kind": "html", "iconSymbol": "brain.head.profile", "iconColor": "indigo"}